INSERT [dbo].[Points] ([PointID], [Title], [Summary], [Description], [CustomerID], [ProductID], [ReportedByID], [AssignedToID], [DateCreated], [StartDate], [DateCompleted], [DateClosed], [Status], [Priority], [Category], [Complexity], [TicketID], [ExpectedDate], [DateSentToQC], [TesterStartDate], [DeveloperRemark], [TesterRemark], [TesterCompleteDate], [SortOrder], [IsVerified], [IsDeadlineNotified], [ExpectedMinutes], [TotalTimeSpent], [PauseTimeMinutes], [LastActionTime], [SupportStartDate], [SupportCompleteDate], [SupportTimeSpent], [SupportPauseTime], [SupportLastActionTime], [IsSupportPaused], [SupportRemark], [IsDeveloperPaused], [VerificationStatus], [ToDoDate], [MergeAssignedToID], [DateSentToMerge], [DateSupportVerified], [DateTicketVerified], [AdminRemark], [Module], [SubModule]) VALUES (294, N'Client Inventory ', N'Return To Stock', N'UI/UX Issue ( Client Inventory --> Return To Stock)

1. Button Styling

Just like the earlier screens, Create (green), Edit (orange), Delete (red), and Show List (blue) all have different colors and sizes. This makes the UI visually noisy and inconsistent.

"Refresh" is in a different style (dark green, rounded) compared to the rest.

2. Alignment Issues

The “From Date” and “To Date” fields are not perfectly aligned vertically with the “Refresh” button.

“Return to Stock” link is right-aligned but visually unbalanced, looking almost detached from the rest of the layout.

3. Font & Spacing

Table header font size and button font size differ noticeably, which breaks consistency.

Padding inside table headers is uneven (some headers look cramped).

4. Date Range

No input validation if the user selects a "To Date" earlier than the "From Date."

No indication if "Refresh" will clear other filters or only update results.

5. Return to Stock

Appears as a plain text link rather than a styled button. Users may miss it.

6. Top-right Controls

The icons (Save, Export, Cancel) are not intuitive. They need tooltips or text labels.

7. No Bulk Actions

