All production processes should be managed and tracked Roll-wise in the ERP system.
Each production transaction should be linked to a specific Roll Number for complete traceability', 376, 7, 149, NULL, CAST(N'2026-06-24T00:00:00.000' AS DateTime), NULL, NULL, NULL, N'Queue', N'High', N'Customization', N'Simple', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, N'hold', NULL, NULL)
INSERT [dbo].[Points] ([PointID], [Title], [Summary], [Description], [CustomerID], [ProductID], [ReportedByID], [AssignedToID], [DateCreated], [StartDate], [DateCompleted], [DateClosed], [Status], [Priority], [Category], [Complexity], [TicketID], [ExpectedDate], [DateSentToQC], [TesterStartDate], [DeveloperRemark], [TesterRemark], [TesterCompleteDate], [SortOrder], [IsVerified], [IsDeadlineNotified], [ExpectedMinutes], [TotalTimeSpent], [PauseTimeMinutes], [LastActionTime], [SupportStartDate], [SupportCompleteDate], [SupportTimeSpent], [SupportPauseTime], [SupportLastActionTime], [IsSupportPaused], [SupportRemark], [IsDeveloperPaused], [VerificationStatus], [ToDoDate], [MergeAssignedToID], [DateSentToMerge], [DateSupportVerified], [DateTicketVerified], [AdminRemark], [Module], [SubModule]) VALUES (5750, N'Production', N'Production', N'Production Entry Tolerance Requirement
The system is currently restricting production entry based on the calculated Running Meter (RM).
A tolerance should be provided to allow production entries slightly higher than the calculated RM quantity.

Example:

Roll Quantity: 2,000 RM
Expected Production: 20,000 Pcs
The system should allow entry of 20,300 Pcs (or a defined tolerance percentage) instead of restricting the entry to exactly 20,000 Pcs.
This tolerance is required because actual production may vary slightly due to machine settings and operational conditions.
