Additionally, for the Packing Slip print format, the print size currently has to be configured by the developer each time. Could we instead have a Print Size option available in the print screen, allowing users to select the required paper size (e.g., A4, A5, etc.) before printing?', 112, 7, 166, 156, CAST(N'2026-06-27T00:00:00.000' AS DateTime), NULL, NULL, NULL, N'PendingSupport', N'Medium', N'Improvement', N'Simple', 3905, CAST(N'2026-06-27T02:48:00.000' AS DateTime), CAST(N'2026-06-27T05:05:29.723' AS DateTime), NULL, N'Complete', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 0, 20, 0, 0, CAST(N'2026-06-27T15:25:43.170' AS DateTime), NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, CAST(N'2026-06-27T15:17:31.857' AS DateTime), NULL, NULL, NULL)
INSERT [dbo].[Points] ([PointID], [Title], [Summary], [Description], [CustomerID], [ProductID], [ReportedByID], [AssignedToID], [DateCreated], [StartDate], [DateCompleted], [DateClosed], [Status], [Priority], [Category], [Complexity], [TicketID], [ExpectedDate], [DateSentToQC], [TesterStartDate], [DeveloperRemark], [TesterRemark], [TesterCompleteDate], [SortOrder], [IsVerified], [IsDeadlineNotified], [ExpectedMinutes], [TotalTimeSpent], [PauseTimeMinutes], [LastActionTime], [SupportStartDate], [SupportCompleteDate], [SupportTimeSpent], [SupportPauseTime], [SupportLastActionTime], [IsSupportPaused], [SupportRemark], [IsDeveloperPaused], [VerificationStatus], [ToDoDate], [MergeAssignedToID], [DateSentToMerge], [DateSupportVerified], [DateTicketVerified], [AdminRemark], [Module], [SubModule]) VALUES (5849, N'Paper Issue – Incorrect Department Mapping for Multi-Content Jobs', N'Item Issue Without Picklist', N'For jobs containing multiple contents (e.g., Cover and Pages in a Perfect Binding Book), paper may be issued to different departments based on the production flow. For example, the Cover may be issued to the Cutting department while the Pages are issued to the Printing department.

Currently, during paper issue, the ERP assigns the same department to all contents and does not retain the department selected individually for each content. As a result, both contents may incorrectly display the same department (e.g., Printing), even though paper was issued to different departments.

Kindly review and correct the department mapping so that each content reflects its respective issue department accurately. Reference screenshots have been provided for better understanding and verification of the issue.', 180, 7, 213, 182, CAST(N'2026-06-27T00:00:00.000' AS DateTime), NULL, NULL, CAST(N'2026-07-04T02:21:40.000' AS DateTime), N'Closed', N'Medium', N'Bug', N'Simple', 3902, CAST(N'2026-06-27T01:13:00.000' AS DateTime), CAST(N'2026-07-02T23:59:48.407' AS DateTime), NULL, N'done', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 0, 20, 0, 0, CAST(N'2026-07-03T12:29:40.967' AS DateTime), NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, CAST(N'2026-06-27T13:42:48.237' AS DateTime), NULL, NULL, NULL)
