A **BF (Burst Factor)** field is required in the **Rate Master** page for proper rate management.

The same paper/reel with the same GSM may have different costs based on its **BF (Burst Factor)**. Therefore, the system should provide a BF field to distinguish and manage rates accordingly.

The field should be configurable as either a **dropdown** or an **input field**, based on the existing system design and implementation standards.
', 112, 7, 213, 156, CAST(N'2026-07-18T00:00:00.000' AS DateTime), NULL, NULL, CAST(N'2026-07-31T13:07:24.263' AS DateTime), N'Closed', N'Medium', N'Improvement', N'Simple', 4163, CAST(N'2026-07-18T12:14:00.000' AS DateTime), CAST(N'2026-07-20T11:13:50.527' AS DateTime), NULL, N'done', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 0, 20, 14, 0, CAST(N'2026-07-18T13:10:42.057' AS DateTime), NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, CAST(N'2026-07-18T12:12:33.207' AS DateTime), NULL, NULL, NULL)
